From a1544f5b17253f41f663873669b791df102bb364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 06:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the query and key masks in cross_attention instead of
 multiplying them

The attention bias multiplied the two mask terms:

    bias = 1e9 * (mask_q - 1.0)[..., None, :, None]
               * (mask_k - 1.0)[..., None, None, :]

(m - 1) is 0 for a valid position and -1 for a padded one, so the product is 0
whenever either side is valid. A valid query therefore received bias 0 on every
key, padded keys included, and no key was ever masked; the only non-zero entries
were +1e9 on fully padded pairs. self_attention in the same file builds its bias
correctly, by adding.

Padded key slots carry zeroed keys and values, but they still take softmax mass
from the real keys, and the pair bias on those slots is non-zero, so it steers
that mass. The window packing in AtomCrossAtt.compute_features only clamps
windows back inside the real-atom range when there are at least 128 real heavy
atoms, so this fires on smaller inputs: for a 5-residue peptide 98 of the 128
key slots are padding and unmasked, taking a mean 0.76 of the softmax mass for
every valid query. The atom transformer runs in the diffusion encoder and
decoder at every denoising step, so this moves predicted coordinates.

Add the two terms. The query term is redundant, since padded query rows are
zeroed afterwards, but keeping it makes the intent explicit and matches the
shape comment.
---
 src/alphafold3/model/network/diffusion_transformer.py | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/alphafold3/model/network/diffusion_transformer.py b/src/alphafold3/model/network/diffusion_transformer.py
index 2148f26..61b2e8c 100644
--- a/src/alphafold3/model/network/diffusion_transformer.py
+++ b/src/alphafold3/model/network/diffusion_transformer.py
@@ -285,11 +285,9 @@ def cross_attention(
   assert len(mask_q.shape) == len(x_q.shape) - 1, f'{mask_q.shape}, {x_q.shape}'
   assert len(mask_k.shape) == len(x_k.shape) - 1, f'{mask_k.shape}, {x_k.shape}'
   # bias: ... x heads (1) x query x key
-  bias = (
-      1e9
-      * (mask_q - 1.0)[..., None, :, None]
-      * (mask_k - 1.0)[..., None, None, :]
-  )
+  bias = (1e9 * (mask_q - 1.0))[..., None, :, None] + (
+      1e9 * (mask_k - 1.0)
+  )[..., None, None, :]
 
   x_q = adaptive_layernorm(x_q, single_cond_q, name=f'{name}q')
   x_k = adaptive_layernorm(x_k, single_cond_k, name=f'{name}k')
